# SentinelAI — Environment Variables (example)

Copy to `.env` locally. **Never commit real `.env` files.**

```bash
# --- AI Gateway (Milestone 5) — not active until configured ---
SENTINEL_AI_PROVIDER=none
SENTINEL_AI_ENDPOINT=
SENTINEL_AI_MODEL=
SENTINEL_AI_API_KEY=

# --- Optional threat intelligence (Milestone 6+) ---
# When unset, the product must display: "Local analysis only."
SENTINEL_TI_VIRUSTOTAL_API_KEY=
SENTINEL_TI_URLHAUS_ENABLED=false
SENTINEL_TI_ABUSEIPDB_API_KEY=

# --- Cloud API (Milestone 4+) ---
SENTINEL_API_BASE_URL=
SENTINEL_API_CLIENT_ID=
SENTINEL_API_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- VPN (Milestone 8) — infrastructure not configured by default ---
SENTINEL_VPN_ENABLED=false
SENTINEL_VPN_API_BASE_URL=
```

If a provider is unset, SentinelAI must tell the user the truth about capabilities.
